dict(i=33, title="CLIAVE Promotion at the Close-out Meeting of the Ministry of Agriculture Projects on the Conservation of Genetic Resources in Serbia", body=[
"The close-out meeting of the projects of the Ministry of Agriculture on the conservation of genetic resources in Serbia served as a great opportunity to promote the CLIAVE project. Indigenous breeds can play a significant role in mitigating and adapting to climate change, which was emphasized at this meeting. The meeting was held on September 19, 2022 at the Institute of Molecular Genetics and Genetic Engineering (IMGGE), University of Belgrade, in the presence of representatives of the Ministry of Agriculture, agronomists, students and researchers, who were invited to follow the project's activities through the website and social networks."]),
dict(i=34, title="CLIAVE in the Media", body=[
"On the occasion of the launch of the CLIAVE project, Dr. Ljiljana Samolovac was a guest of the agro-show \"Plodno i rodno\" on B92 television, where she spoke about the importance and impact of climate change on agriculture. The importance of this interaction in the field of animal husbandry was particularly highlighted, as well as the need to raise awareness and strengthen the competencies of all employees in the agricultural sector, including future experts – students – through projects such as CLIAVE."],
 links=[["Watch the TV agro-show on B92 (0:15–0:33)","https://b92.tv/video/plodno-i-rodno/plodno-i-rodno-18-09-2022-2215955"]]),
dict(i=35, title="CLIAVE Promotion at the Faculty of Agriculture – University of Belgrade", body=[
"At the very beginning of the new academic year, on September 13, 2022, a meeting was held at the Faculty of Agriculture, University of Belgrade, to which students and experts from the advisory services of Serbia were invited to learn about the CLIAVE project. After the presentation, brochures were distributed to the attendees and they were informed about the possibilities of following news through the website and social networks."]),
dict(i=36, title="CLIAVE Presented at Workshops in Vranje, Leskovac, Pirot and Knjaževac", body=[
"Agronomists and farmers from four regions of Serbia were introduced to the CLIAVE project at promotional events held as part of workshops from September 7 to 9, 2022, in the agricultural advisory services in Vranje, Leskovac, Pirot and Knjaževac. The professional and general public was informed about it through the local media."],
 links=[["CLIAVE in Pirot (YouTube)","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=56tCPS9r0H0"],["CLIAVE in Knjaževac (YouTube)","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wxw42pCox0g"]]),
dict(i=37, title="CLIAVE on the Website and Social Media of the Faculty of Agriculture and Technology (Czech Republic)", body=[
"The CLIAVE project was introduced on the website and social media of the Faculty of Agriculture and Technology, University of South Bohemia. The project (2021-1-TR01-KA220-VET-000032974) is supported by the European Union and the Turkish National Agency within the Erasmus+ programme under the action Cooperation partnerships in vocational education and training. Within the project, the Faculty of Agriculture and Technology deals with the topic of Climate Resilient Cropping Systems."]),
dict(i=38, title="Within the Scope of the Project, an Event Was Held in Yalova", body=[
"On July 29, 2022, a meeting was organized as part of the CLIAVE project for students doing their internship at the Atatürk Horticultural Central Research Institute. A total of 18 university students studying agriculture at 11 different universities in Türkiye attended the meeting. Project coordinator Dr. Erdinç Uysal first gave a presentation about the effects of climate on agriculture. He then informed the students about the CLIAVE project and explained how to use the CLIAVE Learning Management System (C-LMS), which was then in preparation.",
"The meeting closed with a Q&A session."]),
dict(i=39, title="Kick-off Meeting", body=[
"The Climate Focused Agricultural Vocational Education project (2021-1-TR01-KA220-VET-000032974) is supported by the European Union and the Turkish National Agency within the Erasmus+ programme under the action Cooperation partnerships in vocational education and training. The project is coordinated by the Atatürk Horticultural Central Research Institute with partners from Türkiye (Bilecik Şeyh Edebali University), the Czech Republic (University of South Bohemia), Slovenia (Institute of Agriculture and Forestry Maribor), Serbia (Institute for Animal Husbandry) and Romania (Iași University of Life Sciences).",
"The project opening ceremony was held with the participation of the Governor of Yalova, Muammer Erol, on 8 June 2022, together with the project partners. During the three-day project meeting, plans were made and information was exchanged with the project partners on how to proceed in the next stages of the project."]),
dict(i=40, title="CLIAVE at the \"Another World is Possible\" Nature, Science, Art and Sports Festival", body=[
"Çınarcık Municipality, together with the Çınarcık District Directorate of National Education and the TEMA Foundation, organized a nature, science, art and sports festival in Çınarcık for Environmental Protection Week. The festival offered informative activities on climate change, beekeeping, biodiversity, medicinal plants and herbs and trekking, as well as hands-on workshops such as nature-friendly cleaning, waste-free living, paper making, model airplanes and ceramics. The project team continued its promotion activities at the festival on June 4, 2022."]),
dict(i=41, title="CLIAVE at Yalova EkoFest", body=[
"CLIAVE participated in the Yalova Environmental Festival, held from May 30 to June 1, 2022 and organized by the Municipality of Yalova to raise awareness. Student groups who visited our stand were informed about the project and leaflets were distributed."]),
dict(i=42, title="CLIAVE Project Started", body=[
"The CLIAVE project started with the 1st online transnational project meeting on 8 March 2022. In this meeting the project teams came together and went through the project form together."]),
